                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "27bcc7a0-7c62-4e53-a9f8-1a4406e0bd6f",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cats'-paws"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14ed4b9e-130c-3367-b251-21450b01f73b",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A paw of a cat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "05c8e4e8-4c9d-36dc-aeca-f92d7ad738b9",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who acts in another's interest, (properly) unknowingly or through trickery."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eca0fb2f-940b-4ccf-8e55-2dcd8cceb30c",
                                "sense_id": "05c8e4e8-4c9d-36dc-aeca-f92d7ad738b9",
                                "text": "To take the Cat by the foote, and therewith rake the coales out of the Ouen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f3df627-dbe0-4d4e-93b6-d94cd3d1a1ea",
                                "sense_id": "05c8e4e8-4c9d-36dc-aeca-f92d7ad738b9",
                                "text": "These he useth as the Monkey did the Cats paw, to scrape the nuts out of the fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "705ee3fb-ed8d-4f87-a12d-3f9b72901ce2",
                                "sense_id": "05c8e4e8-4c9d-36dc-aeca-f92d7ad738b9",
                                "text": "Cat's-paw, common in vulgar speech, but not in writing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fda41eb-082f-4cad-9af6-df4605c85929",
                                "sense_id": "05c8e4e8-4c9d-36dc-aeca-f92d7ad738b9",
                                "text": "Eddie Mars was behind Geiger, protecting him and using him for a cat's-paw."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b5d072-1886-4825-941b-4b0cddd4f749",
                                "sense_id": "05c8e4e8-4c9d-36dc-aeca-f92d7ad738b9",
                                "text": "And for a third thing, Johnson never seemed like he was intent on blowing up NATO because he was a Russian cat’s paw."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c3d5e37-dc5f-394d-b6cd-d19526051e28",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A minor breeze that ripples the surface of a body of water."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d4f6079-86d8-45ad-9d07-263ae7cad3ad",
                                "sense_id": "5c3d5e37-dc5f-394d-b6cd-d19526051e28",
                                "text": "Cats-paw, a light air of wind perceived... by the impression made on the surface of the sea, which it sweeps very lightly, and then decays."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66d185b0-96f6-493c-ae3a-e3d4735f9c30",
                                "sense_id": "5c3d5e37-dc5f-394d-b6cd-d19526051e28",
                                "text": "No, not a cat’s paw anywhere:\nHold up your finger in the air\nYou could n’t feel a breath;\nFor why, in yonder storm that burst,\nThe wind that blew so hard at first\nHad blown itself to death."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71864cdc-376f-4eb2-aa6b-cbe2f13d393b",
                                "sense_id": "5c3d5e37-dc5f-394d-b6cd-d19526051e28",
                                "text": "“Now,” said Hands, “look there; there’s a pet bit for to beach a ship in. Fine flat sand, never a cat’s paw, trees all around of it, and flowers a-blowing like a garding on that old ship.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c7a0a6d-a546-4776-9117-338ee6e51bfc",
                                "sense_id": "5c3d5e37-dc5f-394d-b6cd-d19526051e28",
                                "text": "There was very little wind, though now and again a catspaw hurrying from the south helped them on their way and darkened the smooth small waves."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e94c3877-39d6-38ae-a8aa-19ab46a157d7",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A twisting variant of the lark's-foot hitch which forms two small bights used to hook a pair of tackles to a rope."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "580933e2-14e2-40d7-9934-10f00714113c",
                                "sense_id": "e94c3877-39d6-38ae-a8aa-19ab46a157d7",
                                "text": "...when the mate came to shake the catspaw out of the down-haul..."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f8c149e-f870-3980-b236-be43a05dbec5",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that comes down quickly upon a victim in the manner of a cat's paw."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncommon"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb5e749f-9481-4015-96fb-13ace9e02c13",
                                "sense_id": "3f8c149e-f870-3980-b236-be43a05dbec5",
                                "text": "[T]hese Florentines [...] / In hungry pride and gainful cowardice, / [...] / Quick cat's-paws on the generous stray-away."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d71dcd09-a0f7-35c5-8f85-f40aad2c997e",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small crowbar with a handle at a right angle to a blade with a V-shaped notch, principally used by carpenters to remove nails."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3ce4c66-25bb-460c-afb4-96d1bd3623c1",
                                "sense_id": "d71dcd09-a0f7-35c5-8f85-f40aad2c997e",
                                "text": "Filed Dec. 13, 1952. Cat's Paw. For Hand Tools for Pulling Nails and Spikes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "91836b9c-858a-302a-a1fa-c05a2a8c7201",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A metal set of claws worn over the hand or wielded in the hand used to remove skin and flesh."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe5ef26a-6940-3c18-9fae-4a65e3cd9ffa",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A supervisor whose reliance on a subordinate's analysis is so complete as to render him or her liable for the subordinate's animus or other misconduct towards a third employee."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "563c3c0b-0919-3df3-b425-98ca8c7a65f4",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of several species of North American freshwater mussels of the genus Epioblasma, especially E. obliquata."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2775fa46-f11a-3137-a0e8-5f8c65d3408e",
                        "entry_id": "7279c28c-07e3-3a77-991b-1057d8bbb982",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of several species of Australian bloodworts of the genus Anigozanthos, especially A. humilis."
                        ],
